# Montage I/O Time Analysis
# Date: 2026-04-09
# Dataset: 208 real 2MASS J-band FITS images (small size)
# Method: strace -f -T -ttt (follow forks, time all syscalls)
# Syscalls traced: read, write, openat, close, lseek, pread64, pwrite64, mmap, munmap, fstat, stat, lstat
# Host: PNNL Deception, AMD EPYC, BeeGFS storage, single login-node run
#
# ─── I/O time calculation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   wall_time     = elapsed wall-clock time (bash date +%s.%N before/after)
#   threads       = unique PID count in strace output (fork-following via -f)
#   io_sum        = sum of all syscall durations across all traced PIDs
#   io_per_thread = io_sum / threads (approximates wall-clock I/O impact)
#   io_pct        = (io_per_thread / wall_time) × 100
#
# Note: Montage binaries are single-threaded (no OpenMP/pthread), so
# threads=1 for all stages in this measurement. The calculation remains
# general and can be applied to multi-threaded tools.
#
# Columns: task_name  wall_time  threads  io_sum  io_per_thread  io_percentage

=== Stage 1: mImgtbl (raw image catalog, serial) ===
mImgtbl_raw          wall=   4.275s  threads= 1  io_sum=   0.677s  io_per_thread=   0.677s  io_pct= 15.84%

