=== Stage 10: mAdd (final mosaic coaddition, serial) ===
mAdd                 wall=   3.548s  threads= 1  io_sum=   2.637s  io_per_thread=   2.637s  io_pct= 74.00%


# ─── Summary Table ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Stage                 Wall Time    I/O Time    I/O %    Classification
#   ──────────────────    ─────────    ────────    ─────    ─────────────────
#   mImgtbl (raw)           4.275s       0.677s    15.8%    Metadata-heavy
#   mProject                3.033s       0.008s     0.3%    Compute-bound ★
#   mImgtbl (projected)     0.775s       0.016s     2.1%    Fast metadata
#   mOverlaps               0.500s       0.005s     1.0%    CPU (geometry)
#   mDiff                   0.027s       0.006s    22.2%    Very short (absolute I/O tiny)
#   mFitExec                5.628s       0.219s     3.9%    CPU (regression)
#   mBgModel                1.190s       0.002s     0.2%    CPU (iterative)
#   mBackground             0.009s       0.001s     5.0%    Very short
#   mImgtbl (corrected)     0.767s       0.016s     2.1%    Fast metadata
#   mAdd                    3.548s       2.637s    74.0%    I/O-bound ★
#
#
# ─── Key Findings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. mProject (the dominant parallel stage, ~208 calls × 3s per call) is
#    99.7% COMPUTE-BOUND. Reprojection is pure CPU work (coordinate
#    transforms + pixel interpolation).
#
# 2. mAdd is the primary I/O-bound Montage stage (74% I/O). It reads all
#    corrected FITS files sequentially to build the final mosaic.
#
# 3. mImgtbl stages spend 2-16% on I/O (metadata reads + catalog writes).
#
# 4. Short-lived stages (mDiff, mBackground) show higher I/O% because their
#    absolute compute time is tiny. In absolute terms, their I/O is
#    negligible (6ms and 1ms respectively).
#
# 5. mFitExec does a serial loop over ~1022 diff files and spends ~4% on
#    I/O, the rest on least-squares plane fitting.
#
#
# ─── Implications for DPM Evaluation ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Montage total runtime is dominated by:
#   • mProject:  ~208 × 3s = ~624s sequential (parallelized across nodes)
#   • mAdd:      ~3.5s but I/O-bound
#
# Per-call I/O percentages:
#   • mProject: 0.3% → storage choice has negligible per-call impact
#   • mAdd:     74%  → direct benefit from faster storage
#
# HOWEVER, at parallel scale (e.g., 208 mProject calls simultaneously hitting
# shared BeeGFS), the aggregate I/O contention becomes significant. Each
# individual mProject waits on the same storage bandwidth, effectively
# serializing the small per-call I/O. This explains why BeeGFS vs SSD vs
# tmpfs show measurable total-runtime differences despite mProject being
# 99.7% compute-bound in isolation.
#
# For DPM storage tier selection, the critical factors are:
#   1. mAdd's read bandwidth from storage (74% I/O per call)
#   2. Aggregate parallel mProject I/O contention (per-call 0.3% × 208 concurrent)
#   3. Metadata operations in mImgtbl (directory scans)
